		<chapter num="78">
			<heading>
				Psalm 78
			</heading>
			<heading>
				Tell the Coming Generation
			</heading>
			<heading>
				A Maskil(1) of Asaph.
			</heading>
			<begin-paragraph>
			</begin-paragraph>
			<v n="1">incline your ears to the words of my mouth!</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078002">
			</marker>
			<v n="2">I will utter dark sayings from of old,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078003">
			</marker>
			<v n="3">fathers have told us.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078004">
			</marker>
			<v n="4">the wonders that he has done.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078005">
			</marker>
			<v n="5">to teach to their children,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078006">
			</marker>
			<v n="6">and arise and tell them to their children,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078007">
			</marker>
			<v n="7">keep his commandments;</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078008">
			</marker>
			<v n="8">whose spirit was not faithful to God.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078009">
			</marker>
			<v n="9">turned back on the day of battle.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078010">
			</marker>
			<v n="10">but refused to walk according to his law.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078011">
			</marker>
			<v n="11">the wonders that he had shown them.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078012">
			</marker>
			<v n="12">the fields of Zoan.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078013">
			</marker>
			<v n="13">stand like a heap.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078014">
			</marker>
			<v n="14">and all the night with a fiery light.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078015">
			</marker>
			<v n="15">and gave them drink abundantly as from the deep.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078016">
			</marker>
			<v n="16">and caused waters to flow down like rivers.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078017">
			</marker>
			<v n="17">rebelling against the Most High in the desert.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078018">
			</marker>
			<v n="18">by demanding the food they craved.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078019">
			</marker>
			<v n="19">spread a table in the wilderness?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078020">
			</marker>
			<v n="20">or provide meat for his people?”</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078021">
			</marker>
			<v n="21">his anger rose against Israel,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078022">
			</marker>
			<v n="22">and did not trust his saving power.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078023">
			</marker>
			<v n="23">opened the doors of heaven,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078024">
			</marker>
			<v n="24">the grain of heaven.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078025">
			</marker>
			<v n="25">in abundance.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078026">
			</marker>
			<v n="26">and by his power he led out the south wind;</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078027">
			</marker>
			<v n="27">the sand of the seas;</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078028">
			</marker>
			<v n="28">all around their dwellings.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078029">
			</marker>
			<v n="29">craved.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078030">
			</marker>
			<v n="30">while the food was still in their mouths,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078031">
			</marker>
			<v n="31">the young men of Israel.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078032">
			</marker>
			<v n="32">despite his wonders, they did not believe.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078033">
			</marker>
			<v n="33">and their years in terror.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078034">
			</marker>
			<v n="34">they repented and sought God earnestly.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078035">
			</marker>
			<v n="35">redeemer.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078036">
			</marker>
			<v n="36">lied to him with their tongues.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078037">
			</marker>
			<v n="37">they were not faithful to his covenant.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078038">
			</marker>
			<v n="38">and did not stir up all his wrath.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078039">
			</marker>
			<v n="39">a wind that passes and comes not again.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078040">
			</marker>
			<v n="40">the desert!</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078041">
			</marker>
			<v n="41">the Holy One of Israel.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078042">
			</marker>
			<v n="42">or the day when he redeemed them from the foe,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078043">
			</marker>
			<v n="43">the fields of Zoan.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078044">
			</marker>
			<v n="44">so that they could not drink of their streams.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078045">
			</marker>
			<v n="45">frogs, which destroyed them.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078046">
			</marker>
			<v n="46">and the fruit of their labor to the locust.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078047">
			</marker>
			<v n="47">and their sycamores with frost.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078048">
			</marker>
			<v n="48">and their flocks to thunderbolts.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078049">
			</marker>
			<v n="49">destroying angels.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078050">
			</marker>
			<v n="50">but gave their lives over to the plague.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078051">
			</marker>
			<v n="51">Ham.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078052">
			</marker>
			<v n="52">and guided them in the wilderness like a flock.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078053">
			</marker>
			<v n="53">the sea overwhelmed their enemies.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078054">
			</marker>
			<v n="54">won.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078055">
			</marker>
			<v n="55">and settled the tribes of Israel in their tents.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078056">
			</marker>
			<v n="56">and did not keep his testimonies,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078057">
			</marker>
			<v n="57">a deceitful bow.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078058">
			</marker>
			<v n="58">idols.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078059">
			</marker>
			<v n="59">and he utterly rejected Israel.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078060">
			</marker>
			<v n="60">the tent where he dwelt among mankind,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078061">
			</marker>
			<v n="61">glory to the hand of the foe.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078062">
			</marker>
			<v n="62">vented his wrath on his heritage.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078063">
			</marker>
			<v n="63">marriage song.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078064">
			</marker>
			<v n="64">widows made no lamentation.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078065">
			</marker>
			<v n="65">like a strong man shouting because of wine.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078066">
			</marker>
			<v n="66">he put them to everlasting shame.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078067">
			</marker>
			<v n="67">he did not choose the tribe of Ephraim,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078068">
			</marker>
			<v n="68">loves.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078069">
			</marker>
			<v n="69">like the earth, which he has founded forever.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078070">
			</marker>
			<v n="70">and took him from the sheepfolds;</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078071">
			</marker>
			<v n="71">inheritance.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078072">
			</marker>
			<v n="72">guided them with his skillful hand.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19078073">
			</marker>
			<end-paragraph>
			</end-paragraph>
